THOUGHT: `server` is annotated @Nullable because it can be set to null in dispose(), so NullAway flags direct dereference in accept(). The minimal fix is to add a local non-null check (and throw if disposed) before calling accept(), without changing other behavior. Then I should run the compile to ensure the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '82,86c\  @Override
  public Socket accept(SocketHints hints) {
    try {
      java.net.ServerSocket localServer = server;
      if (localServer == null) {
        throw new GdxRuntimeException("Error accepting socket: server socket is disposed.");
      }
      return new NetJavaSocketImpl(localServer.accept(), hints);
    } catch (Exception e) {
      throw new GdxRuntimeException("Error accepting socket.", e);
    }
  }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/net/NetJavaServerSocketImpl.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -E "NullAway|errors" new_build_output.log | tail -20```

